Subject: Profile type notes forget freed and moved shapes

What this does
  - The profile build's type notes (aot_notes) name shapes by address without a reference. A shape that is freed (js_free_shape0), whose allocation is replaced (resize_properties) or compacted now marks its note dead and turns every note slot that named it as the value shape into "several" (aot_note_shape_freed). Two open-addressed tables find a shape's note and the shapes noted as value shapes; a dead note keeps its place in the probe chain, so a new shape at the same address starts a new note.

Why we need it
  In a 300 s typescript profile run the dump at JS_FreeRuntime (aot_dump_contents) read nt->sh->aot_prof_seen of a shape that was freed or moved: SIGSEGV, so octane.sh reported "typescript FAIL profile". Profile builds only (QJS_AOT_PROFILE).

Soundness
  No reference is taken, so shape copy-on-write behaviour in the profile run is unchanged. A shape edited or moved loses its notes (its facts are stale anyway); no address is read after its free, and address reuse cannot attribute a stale note to a new shape.

